## Ticket #4471: dates parse mm/dd in eu locales

Analysis of 427 reports merged into ticket #4471 revealed three distinct problems for booking dates landing on the wrong day.

## Problems Found

### 1. Dates offset by exactly one day
**Reports covered:** 5

In specific situations, dates shift by exactly one day. Examples include invites arriving the day before booking, or same meeting shown as Tuesday in one timezone and Monday in another.

**GitHub issue:** [Dates offset by exactly one day in specific cases](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/9)

### 2. Date Parser Bug (month-day swap)
**Reports covered:** 388

The date parser reads all dates as MM/DD globally, but tenants in day-first locales write dates as DD/MM. This flips the day and month.

**Affected locales:** en-GB, nl-NL, cs-CZ, it-IT, and others with day-first formatting.

**GitHub issue:** [Date parser reads month-first in day-first locales](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/7)

### 3. Booking-v3 Form Hint Bug
**Reports covered:** 34

The booking-v3 form displays "MM/DD/YYYY" hint in day-first locales. Users follow the hint and type month-first, but the form parser expects day-first input, causing another date flip.

**Affected locales:** Same day-first locales using booking-v3 form.

**GitHub issue:** [Booking-v3 form hint confuses date input in day-first locales](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/8)

## Summary

Three distinct problems cause booking dates to land on the wrong day:
- One-day offset: 5 reports from timezone or boundary edge cases
- Parser month-day swap: 388 reports from parser reading MM/DD in day-first locales
- Form hint mismatch: 34 reports from booking-v3 form showing wrong hint in day-first locales

Total reports analyzed: 427 from April to October 2026.
